# PR #494 (merged, batch 123) — cdz-agent: inbox parser only matches COMPACT json + write_reply omits required `seq`

Mirrored from Copilot inline on merged PR #494 (2 comments), both in
`implementation/seed/crates/cdz-agent/src/main.rs`. Confirmed on trunk. Owner: **v-agent-harness**.
Both break the cdz-agent inbox-loop against REAL fleet inboxes.

## 1. json_string_field matches only the compact `"key":"` needle, but fleet writes PRETTY json (comment 3597724345, line 335)
> The inbox messages produced by `cargo xtask fleet` are pretty-printed via
> `serde_json::to_string_pretty` (e.g. `"body": "..."`), but `json_string_field` looks for the compact
> `"<key>":"` needle. So `body`/`from` parse as empty in real fleet inboxes — the driver sends an empty
> prompt and `--reply-to` usually refuses (empty `from`).

Trunk `main.rs:344`: `let needle = format!("\"{key}\":\"");` — the compact form with NO space after `:`.
Fleet delivers messages pretty-printed (`"from": "..."` with a space — confirmed against real inbox
JSONs). The needle never matches → `body`/`from` → empty. FIX: tolerate optional whitespace around `:`
and before the opening quote (or parse with `serde_json`).

## 2. write_reply omits the required `seq` field (comment 3597724409, line 198)
> `write_reply` claims to emit a fleet-format message but omits the required `seq` field that fleet
> readers (`cargo xtask fleet` / slack-bridge) deserialize. Without `seq`, writing these replies into an
> inbox fails to parse and is left behind unprocessed.

Trunk `main.rs:196`: `write_reply` emits `{"from","to","kind","subject","body"}` — NO `seq`. The fleet
`Message` struct (xtask/src/fleet.rs:556) has `seq: u64` as a REQUIRED (non-Option) field, so serde
rejects a reply lacking it → the reply sits unread. FIX: include a `seq` (metadata-only in the fleet
format — a dummy/0 or a local counter is fine) so existing fleet tooling can deserialize the reply.

## Note
These two together mean the cdz-agent hive loop (`--reply-to`) can neither READ real pretty-printed
inbox messages (#1) nor WRITE a reply the fleet can read back (#2). Worth fixing as one pass.

PR: https://github.com/camshaft/cadenza/pull/494
